  "notes": [
    "JPEG source decoder for the texture importer and the JPEG codec of libtiff (Docs/Design/AssetSystem section 12.11, stage A5g). Developer only: ImageCodec and LibTiff use it, runtime targets do not.",
    "The per-precision wrappers (src/wrapper/*-8.c, -12.c, -16.c) are the translation units; they include the generic sources with BITS_IN_JSAMPLE set. The 12- and 16-bit variants are needed even though ImageCodec rejects those precisions before decoding, because jdmaster.c, jcinit.c and others reference the j12 and j16 functions.",
    "Allocation: jmemrocks.c replaces jmemnobs.c and allocates through the allocator bound to the current thread (RocksJpegBindAllocator); without a binding every allocation fails, so no libjpeg allocation reaches the CRT. client_data is left to the caller (libtiff tif_ojpeg.c uses it).",
    "Errors and messages: rocksjpeg.c installs an error manager whose error_exit and warning (level -1) longjmp back into C, so no C++ frame is skipped, and output_message prints nothing. The default libjpeg error manager paths that print to stderr are never used by ImageCodec. libtiff installs its own error manager for TIFF JPEG.",
    "Built without SIMD (no NASM): the C paths only. The integer DCT results are the same on every host."
  ],
